{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED — independent review of exact head 052db91d7170a8e969959bbd548fe1b160513094 for review request 5aeb6f13, co-signing all six named artifacts: docs 27135611, cmd/gitseq-perf b9330e65, internal/app 8edb7589, internal/kernel 197b00cb, internal/workroom 8390b74d, performance 09e43f70.\n\nARCHITECTURE. Affected layers are kernel, application and the perf harness. The kernel gains one additive contract, Reader.LoadWithProgressStream, and a documented LoadResult change: Events is empty on a streamed full read. docs/reference/architecture.md states that contract in this same head and the docs artifact is published here, so the contract change and its page move together. Verification order is preserved rather than relaxed: loadCheckpointInto authenticates the whole candidate and its suffix before streamCheckpointCandidate replays anything, and the replay re-derives every event through checkpointEventFromPayload, which re-checks the envelope, actor signature, target genesis, causal trailers, payload-tree identity, commit-tree equality, payload ceiling and payload hash. internal/app publishes the folded projection only after the audit succeeds, and refuses a short stream via the streamedEvents != Verification.Events guard. internal/workroom interning is value-identical and changes only backing storage. Contracts preserved.\n\nSECURITY. Trust boundaries examined: checkpoint admission, signature verification, the new callback boundary, and the retained evidence. No weakening found. The duplicate-prefix hazard is handled explicitly: checkpointStreamError is returned rather than falling back to a cold scan with a sink that already received a prefix, and the app resets its provisional folder on the retry path. Nil-ing Dedup in the suffix replay is delivery-only and safe: pass one already ran the full dedup check with the complete map, reads from a nil map do not panic, and intra-suffix collision detection still runs against a fresh additions map. Callback effects are provisional and unpublishable until the whole chain verifies. The retained evidence carries no absolute paths, home directories, email addresses or key material.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION — one finding, non-blocking. This change leaves two dead unexported helpers in internal/kernel/checkpoint.go: validateCompactCheckpoint at line 919 and appendCheckpointEvent at line 533. Each now only delegates to its *Into variant and has zero call sites in production and in tests, and go vet does not catch unused functions. I did not request changes, because the only defect is two unreferenced private helpers with no runtime, behavioural or security effect, while a new head would invalidate and require republishing all six artifacts plus a full re-review. I am filing a follow-up child request so the cleanup is assigned durably rather than lost. The remaining five *Into pairs retain live callers and are not fluff.\n\nGATES, INDEPENDENTLY RUN. I cut my own worktree at the exact head rather than reading codex's. go test -count=1 ./... passes: 27 packages ok, zero failures, internal/docset ok. Green was checked for meaning, not assumed. Mutation one: removing the checkpointStreamError guard makes TestCheckpointStreamFailureDoesNotRetryOrPublishVerifiedCache fail, so the duplicate-prefix property is genuinely pinned. Mutation two, a positive control: an unresolvable citation makes the docset gate fail, so the gate bites. internal/docset and internal/docset/citation_baseline.txt are byte-identical to main, so the green comes from the repair and no baseline entry was added.\n\nCITATION REPAIR. Exactly the ten authorized pages change, every hunk inside the rests_on frontmatter block, prose byte-identical. Across all tracked Markdown, all 67 distinct citations resolve, none of the five retired literals survives anywhere, and zero retired-without-successor citations remain; the 23 retired citations still cited all carry successors. All five successor-aware supersessions project effective in the fold.\n\n500k EVIDENCE. Verified against the raw samples, not taken on trust. The evidence commit 08b7c72c is valid for this head because no Go file changed between them. Every figure in the performance.md table matches the ten primary position-1 samples at the stated precision, with the five diagnostics correctly excluded as the prose claims. Worst 500,000-record peak is 2,709,110,784 bytes, which is 2.523 GiB and 36.9 percent below the 4 GiB envelope, and it is a primary sample. Fifteen samples show zero correctness-versus-trusted digest mismatches. The page correctly separates the harness outcome pass from the target verdict instead of conflating them.\n\nNo change to this head is required. Any change to it invalidates this approval.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:197b00cb71d33a63545022900d78a1dd50c72c01","artifacts":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:27135611d39b18a93dfe4a02780a92bc1b6f0c5d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b9330e654df59e28dd4716d0298415eee37b072b, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8edb75893ac01a3cb8d8c33af63cd5edd36fcfc6, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:197b00cb71d33a63545022900d78a1dd50c72c01, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8390b74d18360c1b552619b2aa764765101e1429, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:09e43f70a71f593b75d7f727a31b24f19d213303","head":"052db91d7170a8e969959bbd548fe1b160513094","verdict":"approved"}}